 **SOURCE-AUDITED LIMITATION.** TWRP was booted only as a transient recovery path. Its `devmem` binary is present, but `/dev/mem` is absent, so a recovery-side MMIO snapshot was not available. No recovery MMIO read was performed and recovery was not patched.
 
+## Corrected decode
+
+`DCFG=0x0008080c` is `DEVSPD=4` (SuperSpeed configuration), `DEVADDR=1`, `NUMP=4`. It is not a High-Speed device configuration.
+
+`DSTS=0x00d38f74` is `CONNECTSPD=4`, `USBLNKST=4` (`SS.Disabled`), `DEVCTRLHLT=1`, `COREIDLE=1`. This is a halted device controller, not an active HS/FS link. A nonzero `SOFFN` field is not evidence of live SOF traffic while the controller is halted.
+
+`DCTL=0x00f00000` has `RUN_STOP=0`.
+
+`DEVTEN=0x47` sets bits 0, 1, 2, and 6. Bit 3 (`ULSTCNGEN` / link-state change) is clear, so link-state events are not enabled. `OSTS=0`.
+
+`QSCRATCH_HS_PHY_CTRL=0x10100000` has both `UTMI_OTG_VBUS_VALID` (bit 20) and `SW_SESSVLD_SEL` (bit 28) set. `QUSB2` `PORT_POWERDOWN` low byte `0x22` has `POWER_DOWN=0`, `PLL_STATUS` low byte `0x20` has `PLL_LOCKED=1`, and `GCC_QUSB2PHY_PRIM_BCR=0`.
+
 ## Interpretation and next candidate
 
-**INFERENCE/HYPOTHESIS.** The measured QUSB2 session-valid bits, PLL lock and non-powered-down state make a dead or unpowered QUSB2 PHY less likely than before; they do not prove cable ownership, host enumeration, endpoint correctness, or a root cause. `DCTL.RUN_STOP=0` and `DSTS.DEVCTRLHLT=1` show that the inherited DWC3 device controller is halted at the time of the snapshot.
+```text
+D7T1_PRIMARY_HYPOTHESIS=QUALCOMM_WRAPPER_QUSB2_PHY_SESSION_OWNERSHIP
+D7T1_ROOT_CAUSE_PROVEN=no
+```
+
+The failed pre-Candidate-1 command log reached the EP0 command path without an exception, a host bus-reset/connect event, or enumeration. That does not uniquely identify QUSB2 power/clock/reset, QSCRATCH session-valid state, DWC3 `RUN_STOP`, the inherited SuperSpeed `DCFG`, EP0 completion decoding, or event-buffer configuration. `ROOT_CAUSE=PHY_OWNERSHIP_PROVEN` is not recorded.
+
+Candidate-2A narrows the first two of those alternatives for this snapshot: the QUSB2 PHY is powered and PLL-locked, and both peripheral-session bits are already set. It does not prove that those bits reflect a real cable session.
+
+**Known-good reference.** On 2026-09-22 the phone was in TWRP with ADB up. `/sbin/devmem` is present and fails with `can't open '/dev/mem'`. No recovery patch was applied. Register meanings are taken from the audited Sony CAF / Linux MSM8996 DWC3 glue, QUSB2 PHY, and Tone DT.
+
+```text
+KNOWN_GOOD_USB_REFERENCE_SOURCE=SONY_CAF_DRIVER_REFERENCE
+```
+
+**Decision gate, not executed.** Case A would require the PHY powered and PLL-locked while `UTMI_OTG_VBUS_VALID` and `SW_SESSVLD_SEL` are absent. Both bits are set, so Case A is not met. Case B would require the PHY powered down or the PLL unlocked. The PHY is powered and the PLL lock bit is set, so Case B is not met. Neither authorized mutation applies.
+
+```text
+RECOMMENDED_CANDIDATE2B=CASE_C
+```
 
-**Recommended Candidate-2B — do not execute automatically:** source-audit a DWC3-only, minimal device-takeover sequence starting from this frozen snapshot. It must retain the exact QSCRATCH, QUSB2 and GCC values as a before/after oracle; avoid PHY clocks, resets and wrapper writes; and separately prove each controlled DWC3 transition before endpoint or DMA work. Candidate-2A is complete evidence collection only, not enumeration.
+No QSCRATCH, QUSB2, DWC3, event-buffer, EP0, or `RUN_STOP` write is authorized from this snapshot. SuperSpeed and the QMP USB3 PHY stay out of scope. DCFG conversion to High-Speed is not part of Candidate-2A.
